arm64: dts: h713: the display MIPS node, enabled on the HY310

sun50i-h713-mips (0231) binds to mips@3061000: the MIPS control block
(mipsloader@3061000 in the stock tree) and, as its second reg, the
core's clock and resets in the CCU, 0x02001600 and 0x0200160c, which the
driver owns raw and does not request (the CCU driver holds its block).
The window is the reservation U-Boot loads display.bin into,
mips-firmware@4b100000.

The node is disabled in the dtsi and enabled in the HY310's tree, where
the restart brought the picture back (08.10.2026). The HY300 Pro and the
HY200 QZ713DF A1 include the HY310's tree and switch it off again. On the
HY300 Pro no restart is on record. On the HY300PRO-G-EU, which uses the
HY200 QZ713DF A1 tree, every earlier reload whose result was looked at
ended black.

The four H713 DTBs, built with the kernel's own cpp and dtc command line,
differ from those of the R1 kernel only by this node and by the phandle
numbers after mips-firmware@4b100000, which now has one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
@@ -46,6 +46,11 @@
 	firmware-name = "h713-arisc.bin", "hy310-edid.bin";
 };
 
+/* The display MIPS restart is measured on the HY310 only. */
+&mips {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
 /* PB5 stays the dtsi's hog here, not the board manager's (see above). */
 &fan_power_hog {
 	status = "okay";
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts
@@ -40,6 +40,11 @@
 	firmware-name = "h713-arisc.bin", "hy310-edid.bin";
 };
 
+/* The display MIPS restart is measured on the HY310 only. */
+&mips {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
 /* PB5 stays the dtsi's hog here, not the board manager's (see above). */
 &fan_power_hog {
 	status = "okay";
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy310.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy310.dts
@@ -51,6 +51,8 @@
  * up the panel. TVTOP stays disabled -- see patch 0033.
  */
 &cpu_comm { status = "okay"; };	/* the driver is built since 01.09. */
+/* the restart of the display MIPS brought the picture back here (08.10.2026) */
+&mips { status = "okay"; };
 &motor_ctr { status = "okay"; };	/* range gate PH14 measured 12.09., see doku/94 */
 &adc_keys { status = "disabled"; };
 &board_mgr { status = "okay"; };	/* temperature + fan speed, see doku/60 */
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -2234,6 +2234,25 @@
 			hwlocks = <&hwspinlock 0>;
 			status = "okay";
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * The MIPS display core: its control block (mipsloader@3061000
+		 * in the stock tree) and, as the second reg, its clock and
+		 * resets in the CCU, 0x02001600 and 0x0200160c (bits 0, 16, 17,
+		 * 18). The driver owns those two words raw, as U-Boot does, and
+		 * does not request them: the CCU driver holds its block, and no
+		 * consumer of CLK_MIPS, CLK_BUS_MIPS or the MIPS resets exists.
+		 * It restarts the core from the window U-Boot loads it into and
+		 * parks it for cpu_comm's standby. Enabled per board, once the
+		 * restart was seen to bring the picture back there.
+		 */
+		mips: mips@3061000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h713-mips";
+			reg = <0x03061000 0x100>, <0x02001600 0x10>;
+			reg-names = "mips", "ccu";
+			memory-region = <&mips_reserved>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
 	};
 
 	/*
